{"component_id_namespace":"ec077a53-0b40-5f21-b1fe-a62094d2476b","component_schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","components":[{"attributes":{"code":"TMC","legacy_node_id":"ks-topeka:tmc:13.20.420","page_type":"section"},"citation":"13.20.420","citation_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/13.20.420","content_hash":"5ff4ed104dcd9d049a88721846bf375f499f9e6bc510b94c3a86aded16ccec10","heading":"Optional permits.","ordinal":0,"parent_source_component_key":null,"schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:13.20.420:section","source_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/13.20.420","text":"(a) The Utilities Director may issue a wastewater discharge permit to any user in accordance with the terms of this article in the following categories:\n(1) A user who requires an estimation of wastewater flow by the Water Pollution Control Division.\n(2) Any person whose wastewater strength is less than the normal range of wastewater strength because of pretreatment, process changes or other reasons.\n(3) Any user identified in the Occupational Safety and Health Administration’s Standard Industrial Classification divisions as follows:\n(i) Division A – Agriculture, Forestry and Fishing.\n(ii) Division B – Mining.\n(iii) Division D – Manufacturing.\n(iv) Division E – Transportation, Communications, Electric, Gas, and Sanitary Services.\n(v) Division I – Services.\n(b) A user in the divisions listed in subsection (a) of this section may be excluded if it is determined that they will introduce only segregated domestic wastes or wastes from sanitary conveniences. (Ord. 20089 § 63, 10-17-17.)","type":"section","workbench_component_id":"14468d2d-6521-5690-841a-996d443c2667"},{"attributes":{"block_kind":"paragraph"},"citation":"13.20.420","citation_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/13.20.420","content_hash":"5a04beb74a9790a07ebbd9cf635b3464454f253bebd14a652d9026c5a1738aa1","heading":null,"ordinal":0,"parent_source_component_